SUMMARY:[Knowledge Representation & Reasoning][Explainability & Interpretab
 ility] KR 2027 - Main-track title and abstract submission deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: International Conference on Principles of Kno
 wledge Representation and Reasoning\nWebsite: https://kr.org/KR2027/\nSou
 rce URL: https://kr.org/KR2027/dates.html\nLocation: Buenos Aires\, Argen
 tina\nTopics: Knowledge Representation & Reasoning\, Explainability & Int
 erpretability\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / formal and symboli
 c AI\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-28\nNotes: The of
 ficial KR 2027 site lists Sep 21-24\, 2027 in Buenos Aires (workshops Sep
  18-20) and AoE (UTC-12) main-track dates\; the main-track call page is n
 ot yet published. The title-and-abstract step is kept as a gate per KR's 
 two-step timetable\, though neither the 2026 nor the 2027 page says it is
  mandatory. No 2027 special tracks are announced yet. M is an editorial e
 stimate.\nScope: Formal and symbolic AI centered on representing knowledg
 e and drawing justified conclusions: knowledge bases\, description and no
 n-classical logics\, ontologies\, non-monotonic reasoning\, argumentation
 \, belief revision\, and reasoning about actions. Learning\, uncertainty\
 , and explanations matter when grounded in knowledge representation or re
 asoning. The last published CFP includes a KR Meets Machine Learning and 
 Explanation track\; this is not a general-purpose ML conference or a conf
 irmed promise of that 2027 track.\nAdditional topics: Machine Learning\, 
 Probabilistic\, Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Planning & Search\nScope source
 s (2026): https://kr.org/KR2026/call_main_track.html\, https://kr.org/KR2
 026/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://kr.org/KR2027/dates.html
END:VEVENT
